    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting explanations based on a student’s level. They can also provide instant feedback, making practice less stressful. For example, they could break down complex problems into simpler steps or suggest alternative approaches if a student gets stuck."
